cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  libmatch: code and result tables for "Library size and sequence
  relatedness confound comparisons between synthetic benchmarks and
  experimental antibody data"
message: >-
  If you use this software or the result tables, please cite both the software
  and the article it accompanies.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Dohun
    family-names: Kim
    email: dohun@etri.re.kr
    affiliation: >-
      Autonomous Intelligence DX Research Section, Electronics and
      Telecommunications Research Institute
  - given-names: Minho
    family-names: Bae
    affiliation: >-
      Autonomous Intelligence DX Research Section, Electronics and
      Telecommunications Research Institute
abstract: >-
  libmatch measures five operational axes of a sequence-label dataset -
  size, structure, dimension, measurement noise and training budget - and
  reports which of them differ between two datasets being compared, or
  cannot be measured from the data as released. The repository also
  holds the scripts and result tables behind the article, with a generated
  reproduction map from every reported number to the script that produced it.
  The matched libraries themselves are not redistributed, because their labels
  are energies computed with Absolut!, whose non-commercial licence grants no
  onward distribution right; their specifications and sha256 digests are
  included instead, with the script that rebuilds them from a reader's own
  licensed download.
keywords:
  - antibody
  - machine learning
  - benchmark
  - dataset comparability
  - reproducibility
  - protein engineering
